" 13194139534304 false] [17592186100607 1145 "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139534304 true] [17592186100608 1100 "Let $C=AB$. What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534304 false] [17592186100608 1100 "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534304 true] [17592186100608 1145 "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $A$ by the $2$nd column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nc_{3